  "Question": "Marie does three equally time-consuming tasks in a row without taking breaks. She begins the first task at \\(1\\!:\\!00\\) PM and finishes the second task at \\(2\\!:\\!40\\) PM. When does she finish the third task?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3{:}10\\) PM",
    "B": "\\(3{:}30\\) PM",
    "C": "\\(4{:}00\\) PM",
    "D": "\\(4{:}10\\) PM",
    "E": "\\(4{:}30\\) PM"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The interval from \\(1{:}00\\) PM to \\(2{:}40\\) PM covers exactly two tasks. It lasts \\(60+40=100\\) minutes. Since the tasks take equal amounts of time, each takes\n\\[\n100\\div2=50\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThe third task ends \\(50\\) minutes after \\(2{:}40\\) PM, which is \\(\\boxed{3{:}30\\text{ PM}}\\), choice B.",
